==> Data Types

=====================================================================================
INT:            Integer type, used for whole numbers.
=====================================================================================
VARCHAR(100):   Variable-length string, up to 100 characters.
=====================================================================================
ENUM:           A string object with a value chosen from a list of permitted values.
                eg. gender ENUM('Male', 'Female', 'Other')
=====================================================================================
DATE:           Stores date values. eg date_of_birth DATE
=====================================================================================
TIMESTAMP:      Stores date and time, automatically set to the current timestamp
                when a row is created.
=====================================================================================
BOOLEAN:        Stores TRUE or FALSE values, often used for flags like is_active.
=====================================================================================
DECIMAL(10, 2): Stores exact numeric data values, useful for financial data.
                The first number is the total number of digits,
                and the second is the number of digits after the decimal point.
=====================================================================================